{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And against the nobles.</b> They are Nadav and Avihu and the elders." "<b>He did not stretch out His hand.</b> From the implication — they were liable to have a hand stretched out against them (Tanchuma, Vayikra Rabbah 20)." "<b>And they beheld the Elohim.</b> They were gazing at Him with a coarse heart, out of eating and drinking — thus is the midrash of Tanchuma; and Onkelos did not translate thus." "<b>Nobles.</b> A term of great ones, as in ״וּמֵאֲצִילֶיהָ קְרָאתִיךָ״ (Isaiah 41), ״וַיָּאצֶל מִן הָרוּחַ״ (Numbers 11), ״שֵׁשׁ אַמּוֹת אַצִּילָה״ (Ezekiel 41)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:18.650119210Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}